From 3122b39369feeee546297726494e76ac29f21db5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:19:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Study guide: keep each line of a working on its own line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The summaries write a derivation one step per line:

    2 − |x − 3| ≤ 0 + 2
    2 − |x − 3| ≤ 2
    y ≤ 2

The markdown renderer folded those into one paragraph, so the guide showed
"2 − |x − 3| ≤ 0 + 2 2 − |x − 3| ≤ 2 y ≤ 2" on one line. Not a derivation,
a string of symbols. Checked all 84 summaries: no multi-line paragraph is a
hard-wrapped sentence, so a newline inside a paragraph is now a line break.

While in there, the other things that made the guide harder to read than
the deck it explains:

- A formula could wrap at its operator ("|x −" / "3| ≥ 0"). Spaces around a
  maths operator are now non-breaking, and the vertical bar (a break-after
  character in Unicode) gets a word joiner, so an expression moves to the
  next line whole.
- A paragraph that is all formula lines is styled as working (left rule,
  monospace-ish weight) so the calculation stands apart from the prose.
- The scope note that opens every summary (a thousand characters about what
  the deck does not cover) now opens collapsed.
- Paragraphs over 400 characters are split at sentence ends into pieces a
  phone screen can hold, same rule as the check explanations.
- 46 lines across 10 summaries were entire quotes wrapped in "..." that the
  renderer showed as literal quote marks around a formula; the marks are
  removed, the text unchanged.

